  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday through next Friday)\nIssued at 1132 PM CDT FRI JUL 24 2026\n\nBy later this morning, the stalled cold front will have finally\npulled north, exiting the region. However, that won't be an end\nto our rain chances on Saturday. Another shortwave is expected to\nride south along the trough still overhead, allowing for one more\norganized shot at shower and thunderstorm chances through today.\nThese rain chances will begin to taper off into Sunday, becoming\na bit more scattered by the morning hours, completely decreasing\nin coverage into the afternoon and evening hours.\n\nBy Monday, a significant pattern shift is still expected to take\nplace, as a stout upper-level ridge works into the region via the\nPlains. High temperatures on Monday will immediately climb into\nthe low to mid-90s, before climbing again on Tuesday into the mid\nto upper-90s. While guidance remains bullish on some pockets of\ntriple-digits, confidence here is low given how much rainfall\nwe've recently received. The ridge will slightly retrograde on\nWednesday, but that will only allow for a slight drop in\nafternoon highs. Anticipated low to mid-90s each day headed into\nnext weekend.\n\n/44/",
